    <h1>Emotion Coding</h1>
    <span class="image main"><img src="images/herbs_main.webp" alt="" /></span>

    <p>Emotion Coding is a wonderful way to release trapped emotions that are accidentally stored in the body during times of emotional overwhelm, trauma and stress. Once trapped, they impede the flow of energy, lymph and circulation and can cause and contribute to dis-ease, presenting in a variety of ways. By identifying and releasing these trapped emotions, we support your body's natural ability to heal and restore balance and flow. We allow them to process, move through and out.</p>

    <p>It works well with Reiki and bodywork or is a great and transformational tool on its own. (It can be a stand-alone phone session or a 25-minute in-person add-on.) As something offered in person or virtually, even friends and family out of the area can access these incredible healing sessions. AND trapping emotions isn't something just humans do- pets that have experienced trauma can benefit greatly from energy healing as well.</p>

    <h2>Some things my clients are saying-</h2>

    <p>"I had been in a pattern of waking up with debilitating anxiety and dread to start my day. I noticed immediate relief and improvement after my session. I've experienced more patience when faced with daily challenges. In the past when I dreamed they were almost exclusively negative or nightmarish. Since my session I have experienced light, playful and happy dreams for the first time I can remember." -A.F., Nebraska</p>

    <p>"Our dog, a feisty French Bulldog (rescue from a traumatic situation), began to noticeably relax after only two sessions. She clearly let her guard down and started letting more of her personality show through. She started playfully engaging with other dogs and wagging her tail, which were both new behaviors. She is noticeably lighter and calmer since the session." -M.B., Colorado</p>

    <p>"I recommend emotional coding to anyone who has difficulty processing emotions, anyone who feels they are emotionally stuck or feeling weighed down with emotions but can't figure out why. It's easy, painless and makes a difference with the way you feel overall." -A.K., Colorado</p>

